THE FIX, added verbatim to src/game/pb/pb_window.c between debugScissor's closing brace and the `#pragma dont_inline off` at what was line 263 (i.e. after debugScissor, before pbProjCalc, while dont_inline is still ON so it is code-generated out-of-line):

static f32 pbAspectRatio(f32 w, f32 h)
{
    PBWINGLOBALS* g = gWinGlobals;
    f32 ratio;

    ratio = (g->current->aspect * w) / h;
    if ((((PBSCREEN*) g->screen)->flags & 2) != 0) {
        ratio = ratio * 2.0f;
    }
    return ratio;
}

It is the aspect step pbProjCalc pastes out inline at its own lines 440-443, in the file's documented Midway paste style (same device and same justification as the existing pbWindowDefaults). It creates EXACTLY ONE new pool literal, 2.0f: the multiply and divide are variable-operand, and `flags & 2` is an integer immediate. Nothing references it, so mwld dead-strips it; claimcheck's .text overshoot measures 0x1904 against the 0x1874 claim and stays a note, not an error (the prior record measured 0x18d4 with only the one earlier helper present; that 0x18d4 is quoted, not remeasured this session).

MECHANISM PROBE THAT PROVED IT FIRST (kept here because it is the minimal reproducer, 4 lines, and it moved the pool on its own):

