TWO AXES WERE MEASURED DEAD BEFORE the helper, and both are recorded here so they are not re-run. (D) THE w2/h2 'SUSPICIOUS RECONSTRUCTION' LEVER NAMED BY THE PRIOR RECORD IS REFUTED, not merely untried: the prior record proposed that pbProjCalc's `zA = (f32) ((PBSCREEN*) g->screen)->w2; zB = (f32) ((PBSCREEN*) g->screen)->h2;` might hide an early 2.0f. It does not. `fnasm.py game/pb/pb_window pbProjCalc 0x0:0x180` shows +0x11c..+0x15c is a plain UNSIGNED-INT-to-float conversion of two integer fields at screen+0x30 and screen+0x34 (lwz / xoris / stw / lfd / fsubs against the 2^52 magic) with no floating literal of any kind. The reconstruction is correct as written and there is no semantic fix hiding there. (E) NO EMITTED CODE IN pbProjCalc CAN CREATE THE 2.0f: `Select-String lbl_80349050|lbl_80349054` over build/GUNE5D/asm/game/pb/pb_window.s shows every use of 2.0f and 0.5f in the WHOLE linked TU lives inside pbProjCalc, first 0.5f load at 0x800C8830 (+0x364) and first 2.0f load at 0x800C88B4 (+0x3e8). Since creation order is parse order and the target's text order equals our unmoved source order (axis A of v1), the 2.0f creator cannot be emitted code that precedes the 0.5f - it has to be code that is generated and then dropped. That is what makes the dead-stripped static the ONLY remaining device, not merely the most likely one.
